PROMPT 9 — ROUTELESS INTELLIGENT BUS REALLOCATION ENGINE
ROLE

Act as a senior algorithm engineer specializing in operations research, resource allocation and emergency transportation optimization.

Continue the existing ROUTELESS project.

OBJECTIVE

Build a deterministic, explainable bus reallocation engine for emergency situations.

INPUTS

Use actual project records:

Operational buses.
Bus capacities.
Available drivers.
Student requests.
Examination deadlines.
Travel times.
Available routes.
Blocked road segments.
Transfer points.
Demand increases.
Vehicle repositioning requirements.
HARD CONSTRAINTS

Never:

Allocate unavailable buses.
Exceed bus capacity.
Allocate buses without available authorized drivers.
Use blocked or unsafe roads.
Assign impossible journeys.
Ignore repositioning time.
Promise unheld seats.
PRIORITY

Use a lexicographic allocation strategy:

Safety and operational feasibility.
Students with imminent examinations.
Other examination students.
Students with earlier arrival deadlines.
Maximum number of feasible on-time journeys.
Minimum total journey time.
Minimum unnecessary transfers.

Do not allow lower-priority optimization objectives to override safety.

ALLOCATION ENGINE

Implement an appropriate deterministic method, such as capacity-constrained matching, min-cost flow or another justified optimization algorithm.

Document the selected algorithm and its limitations.

Separate route calculation from seat allocation.

Track residual capacity after every assignment.

Support reserve vehicles if they are included in the dataset.

RESULTS

Display:

Assigned students.
Unassigned students.
Assigned buses.
Used capacity.
Remaining capacity.
Boarding stops.
Transfer stops.
Estimated arrival times.
Examination priority.
Allocation explanations.
Reasons for unassignment.
CRISIS PERFORMANCE

Test the simultaneous scenario:

Two buses unavailable.
40% additional demand.
One flooded road.
Multiple imminent examinations.
Limited available seats.

Never hardcode successful allocation statistics.

ACCEPTANCE TESTS
Zero capacity violations.
Zero unavailable-bus assignments.
Zero blocked-road assignments.
Driver authorization respected.
Examination priority respected.
Unassigned students explained.
Repeatable deterministic results.
Results match an independent reference test on the defined fixtures.

Integrate the engine into the Crisis Control Center and Student Dashboard.
